--- !u!114 &1235820255
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1235820253}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshProUGUI
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "SAFETY OVERRIDE TRAINING\r\n\r\n  A nuclear reactor's cooling system has
    detected irregular pressure fluctuations. As a two-person safety team, you must
    collaborate to stabilise the pressure gauge before the reactor triggers an automatic\r\n 
    emergency shutdown.\r\n\r\n  Your Role\r\n\r\n  - Supervisor \u2014 You can see
    the pressure gauge with a moving green safe zone and a confirmation button. The
    needle and the Technician's button are not visible to you. Use your laser pointer
    to guide the\r\n  Technician towards the safe zone. When the Technician signals
    they are ready, your button unlocks \u2014 press it to log the reading. A correct
    reading triggers a green indicator. A missed reading triggers a red\r\n  warning
    alert.\r\n  - Technician \u2014 You can see the needle and your signal button.
    The gauge, green zone and Supervisor's button are not visible to you. Use the
    pressure dial to adjust the needle position based on the\r\n  Supervisor's laser
    guidance. When you believe the needle is aligned, press your button to signal
    the Supervisor.\r\n\r\n  Getting Started\r\n  1. Press the controller trigger
    to begin\r\n  2. Put the controller down\r\n  3. Hold your hands in front of
    your eyes to activate hand tracking\r\n"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
